- b229c04 symbols: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 import_edges: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 symbol_refs: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 test_map: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 commits: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 cochange_pairs: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 labelled_touches: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 path_tokens: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 symbol_tokens: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 fts_symbols: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 fts_paths: derived from the repository and its git history; the first index and mine rebuild it
- b229c04 landmines: human_stated rows are owner input (note --kind landmine, built at 59cc05c only); miner kinds are rebuilt from labelled_touches by the mine
- b229c04 human_facts: target_ref is a path (note --file) or empty, never an id
- b229c04 stats_folds: kept with the two fold watermarks, so the fold state matches the carried whisper_audit/corrections seq values (no build of the layout writes it: the fold is a no-op stub)
- b229c04 questions: live answer-drift state (F5-8), and the only record of `correct --missed-question`, which writes no corrections row in any build
- b229c04 classify_state: the catch-up bookmark of each consumer (F5-8); byte offsets into transcripts the rebuild does not change
- b229c04 consumer_state: read-set keys are path:<path> (hook/delivery.ts) and carry as they are; any other key may embed a file or symbol id, and dropping it only lets a fact repeat once (AD-16's safe direction) — no build writes one (every genre returns [])
- b229c04 session_log: the session diagnostics status and log read (FR-M1)
- b229c04 observed_actions: paths, not ids; the live edit set and run state (F5-8)
- b229c04 regret: the regret proxy is not built in any build (hook/handler.ts "SKELETON: G32"); fact_ref may embed ids
- b229c04 whisper_audit: the audit trail (FR-X6) and the genre a correction is booked to; subject_key may embed file or symbol ids (F5-1) and is carried as NULL, which under-seeds a later resume/fork reseed (AD-16's safe direction) — no build writes a non-NULL one
- b229c04 faults: the fault history status reads (FR-M2); ids are ULIDs
- b229c04 whisper_stats: each project's replica, kept consistent with the carried stats_folds (no build of the layout writes it)
